- op: discuss  # 5741
  at: '2026-09-01T23:56:25Z'  # 5741
  by: agent  # 5741
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5741
  clock: 3  # 5741
  nonce: '5741'  # 5741
  message: "SATISFIED on merged dev 7273edb844 (PR: 'fix(rust): a grouped use-list is an import too'), re-running THIS ITEM'S OWN repro on the merged tree with controls in the same run, cold XDG_CACHE_HOME per case.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE (io-boundaries, the item's filed two-arm repro plus four controls):\n  use std::fs::File;            File::open  -> 1 io edge, fs_read   (control, unchanged)\n  use std::fs::{read_to_string, File};      -> 1 io edge, fs_read   (WAS 0 -- the defect)\n  use std::io; io::stdin()                  -> 1 io edge, ipc_recv  (control, unchanged)\n  use std::io::stdin; stdin()               -> 1 io edge, ipc_recv  (control, unchanged)\nThe grouped arm now produces the identical edge identity as the single arm:\nrust:std::fs::File:0-0:open:external_symbol, where it previously emitted\nrust:external:0-0:File..open:external_symbol.\n\nROOT CAUSE, CONFIRMED AS 'SIMPLY ABSENT' -- which was this item's FIRST STEP\n(absent vs mis-keyed). _extract_use_aliases read three use-forms and every one\nis a DIRECT child of use_declaration, so find_child_by_type (direct children\nonly) found them. tree-sitter wraps a grouped list in a scoped_use_list one\nlevel down, so all three lookups missed and the declaration registered ZERO\naliases -- not a wrong key, no key. Replaced with a recursive walk of the\nuse-tree; the prefix is read textually from the node start to the opening brace\nrather than by enumerating node types, because a prefix may be an identifier,\nscoped_identifier, crate, self, super, super::super, or carry a leading '::'.\n\nA/B OVER FIVE RUST REPOS, cold, baseline asserted by GREPPING the runtime file:\n642 -> 754 io chains, +112, ZERO lost. The 'external' sentinel goes to zero on\nboth repos audited for it (openmls 2->0, zellij 7->0). Per repo: zellij +55,\nfirecracker +31, loro +13, openmls +13, just +0 -- 'just' reported because a\nrepo where the fix changes nothing is the honest shape. Rows read back against\nsource: openmls memory_storage/src/persistence.rs (multi-line use std::{...} ->\nFile::open, env::temp_dir), firecracker src/jailer/src/env.rs:5 (use\nstd::fs::{self, File, .., canonicalize} -> canonicalize, which exercises the\n'self' arm), zellij zellij-utils/src/envs.rs:4 (var / set_var).\n\nINSTRUMENT CORRECTION worth recording: the first diff reported 7 'losses' in\nzellij. Keying a chain on (boundary, primitive, src, DST) counts the dst id --\nthe very thing this fix changes -- so each re-identified chain read as one loss\nplus one gain. Re-keyed on the CALL SITE: +112, zero lost.\n\nTHE ITEM'S SECOND QUESTION IS ANSWERED **NO**. The fully-qualified miss does NOT\nshare this cause: std::fs::File::open(..) and std::io::stdin() were re-measured\nAFTER this fix and are STILL 0, because those call sites have no use statement\nfor any quantity of aliases to reach. Converse also holds -- splitting\nFile::open on its last '::' yields module 'File', matching nothing, so a\nsplitter alone would not have fixed this. Filed as INV-<fq> (see isbefore-free\nsibling filed same day).\n\nNOT GATED on v9/v10 despite changing external_symbol ids, and the reasoning is\nrecorded because the gate looks like it applies: WI-marok's gate covers ADR-0024\nstep 7 -- re-vocabularizing values an analyzer already resolved correctly, pure\nre-keying with no correctness gain. Resolving a symbol that previously fell to a\nsentinel is ordinary analyzer-fix business and ships routinely: WI-vutav,\nWI-dizag, INV-linub L3 and WI-doluf each moved edges out of 'external' (caddy\n148, jaeger 580, beads 442) with no scheme bump."  # 5741
